'''Iguanidae Ibilujon''' (超暴獣イビルージョン, ''Chō Bōjū Ibirūjon'', '''Super Violent Beast Ibilujon''') is a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of [[Johnnyleon]] introduced in the [[Continuation Stage]]s of [[Hunter's Map IV]]. It was added in [[Version 12.4 Update|Version 12.4]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Iguanidae Ibilujon
|image = E 650.png
|first appearance = [[Hunter's Map IV]] - [[Purple Crystal Forest]]
|money drop = 2,500¢ - 9,875¢
}}

==Enemy==
Iguanidae Ibilujon is overwhelmingly powerful, even for a Behemoth. It has health surpassing [[Zero Luza]], no blind spot, enough damage to instantly kill almost any conventional meatshield, a typing that greatly reduces the number of viable counters compared to [[Johnnyleon]], and immunity to [[Wave Attack]]s, Knockback and Weaken to counter all efforts of pushing it back without brute force and limit crowd-control options to only rarer yet less effective ones, all while attacking with an Omni Strike that reaches up to 550, but only stopping at 400 range so it can push even deeper and easily reach even Cats trying to stay at farther range. Indeed, rather than being a frontline tank like Johnnyleon, Iguanidae Ibilujon becomes an annoying source of very high-ranged damage from behind enemy lines, then acts as a wall to keep Cats busy until more enemies come out. Well-timed fast meatshields can keep it from having pushing power on its own, but the presence of [[:Category:Enemies with Knockback ability|enemies with knockback abilities]] like [[H. Nah]] or dangerous peons like [[Sir Rel]] can cause it to advance very easily. What makes it all the worse is its [[Counter-Surge]] ability, which is capable of putting out its extreme damage much further than expected should you include [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]] in your formation.

==Strategy==
Iguanidae Ibilujon's Counter-Surge isn't much of an issue as you can simply avoid using Surge Attackers, denying it the chance to generate any [[Surge Attack|Surges]] itself.

This enemy's Omni Strike doesn't let many units attack it safely, so you can only use brute force. [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] and [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] are all powerful [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayer]] [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic specialists]] that can withstand its fire while dealing significant damage. Other Behemoth Slayers such as [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can help with meatshielding/ tanking or providing extra DPS as well. [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] is not as helpful as usual due to the Counter-Surge and Knockback Immunity, but can still inflict decent damage if he connects, since his long cooldown makes duplicated Surges less of a concern.

Though often the less preferable option, a handful of units, such as [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]], can outrange its Omni Strike and whittle it safely. Such units however should still be chosen with Iguanidae Ibiujon's support in mind, as otherwise, they can still advance virtually unopposed thanks to its massive health.

Because of Iguanidae Ibilujon's rapid attack cycle, you'll have to keep your meatshield spam up, or abuse the likes of Research Power Up [[Cat Combo|Combo]]-boosted [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] to ensure it rarely if ever gets to push.

